// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/fpga/wasm_board_ax7203.t27 -- a WASM-executing cell on the ALINX AX7203, one spec
; Board phase (P1) of the epic gHashTag/trinity-fpga#917: AI-generated FPGA hardware that
; executes WASM. Everything between the UART pins is this file; the RTL is generated by t27c
; and never hand-written. The only foreign Verilog in the build is the board top that supplies
; the STARTUPE2 config-oscillator clock and the pins, flagged for the owner label
; owner-approved-foreign on the pull request; the XDC is the existing gf16_clean_ax7203.xdc,
; reused byte for byte.
; -
; WHY. The MVP spec specs/fpga/wasm_interp.t27 proved the interpreter as executable t27: 23
; opcodes, 16 real WASM bodies, 25 checks, icarus green, but no ports and no clock. This cell
; puts that engine on silicon: the same one-opcode-per-clock execution, reached through a real
; UART, on a real board, checked against a golden fixed before the run.
; -
; THE MACHINE. One clock does one thing: a piece of one UART frame, or one WASM opcode. The
; tick body step_all is a plain fn (a task in the generated Verilog, drivable from the tests)
; and on_clock wraps it for the ports. The task keeps blocking assigns, so the tests in this
; file and the silicon clock run the identical sequential body; the sections are ordered so
; every strobe (rxnew, frame_go) is consumed one tick after it is produced. The engine is the
; Verilog-lowerable subset: u32 scalars, u8 bytes, indexed array reads and writes, flat
; if/else opcode dispatch, no loops in the tick body. Programs are the MVP bodies byte for byte
; plus structured control flow (issue #12010): block, loop, br, br_if and br_table over a
; label stack of LABEL_MAX frames, one LEB byte per label. A branch forward skips its bytes
; one per engine step through a syntactic scan that steps over immediates, so an 0x0B inside
; an immediate is never read as an end; FUEL_MAX fetches end a run with ERR_FUEL, so no
; program can hang the link. Still missing: the i64 and float families (beyond the raw-bit
; constants), table.get/set and every linear memory beyond the one 64 KiB page of P5 below; a
; function-level br answers ERR_LABEL (return exists), a label of more than one LEB byte
; answers ERR_LEB. P6 below adds if/else, call, call_indirect and globals.
; THE ALU HAS ONE HOME. The 24 single-clock i32 ALU opcodes (the ten compares, add, sub, the
; eight bitwise/shift/rotate bytes, eqz, clz, ctz, popcnt) are not 24 hand-copied branches:
; alu_arity(op) says how many operands a byte pops (0 = not an ALU byte) and alu_eval(op, a,
; b) is the value it pushes, each written once below. The tick takes one arm for all 24, and
; specs/fpga/wasm_opcodes.t27 `use`s this module and calls the same two functions as its
; oracle, so the table's expected values and the silicon's cannot be two different algorithms
; (issue #12011). The direction is forced: t27c gen-verilog imports only enums and structs
; from a used module, never a function body, so the bodies live in the module that is lowered.
; P2 widens the set: multi-byte signed LEB for i32.const (an operand-fetch submachine in the
; shape of the mul microsequence), drop, select, the unsigned compares, clz/ctz/popcnt,
; shr_u, rotl/rotr, and div/rem signed and unsigned (a 32-clock restoring divider), plus the
; program store loaded over the wire. The MVP spec keeps proving what this cell does not run.
; P5 (issue #12202) adds linear memory, ONE 64 KiB page and nothing larger: i32.load,
; load8_s/u, load16_s/u, i32.store, store8, store16, memory.size and memory.grow. The page is
; `var mem : [MEM_BYTES]u8`, shaped for block RAM: one read OR one write per engine step, the
; address registered (mem_addr) a step before its data is used, and a 2- or 4-byte access is a
; byte-per-step microsequence in the mul/divide shape, little-endian. MEASURED, NOT BLOCK RAM
; YET: yosys 0.67 read_verilog on the generated file answers "Replacing memory \mem with list
; of registers" (the page is written inside the `always @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n)` that
; gen-verilog emits for on_clock; a one-line on_clock probe with a nonblocking write gave the
; same warning; the cause inside yosys is not isolated; compiler gap recorded in the pull
; request). Until that lowering changes the page is 65536 x 8 register bits in synthesis, and
; no claim of block RAM is made here. The memarg (align, then
; offset, two LEB128 u32) has its own submachine: align is read and ignored, a fifth byte of
; either that continues answers ERR_LEB, and so does an offset whose fifth byte carries bits
; above 2^32 (it would wrap). The effective address is base + offset as a 33-bit sum; an
; access of w bytes whose sum exceeds MEM_BYTES - w answers ERR_MEM before any byte is written,
; so there is no wrap and a trapping store leaves the page as it was. memory.size pushes 1;
; memory.grow pops its delta and pushes 0xFFFFFFFF for every delta, 0 included (a documented
; deviation: WASM answers the old size for 0); both carry the reserved memory-index byte,
; which must be 0. Fuel stays one unit per fetch: the extra clocks of a multi-byte access add
; none. The page is declared zero-filled (a repeat, not a 65536-element literal); gen-verilog
; emits no initial block for it, so an iverilog run reads X from a byte nobody wrote and no
; test here reads a byte before it stores it (compiler gap recorded in the pull request).
; P6 (issue #12323) adds if/else, call, return, call_indirect, global.get and global.set on
; the frames that exist. if is a label frame (lab_kind OP_IF) whose block-type byte is read
; and whose condition is popped; a false condition starts the forward scan of #12010 in
; sc_mode 1, which stops at the matching else (class 7, only when sc_n is 1) or at the
; matching end; an else reached by falling through the then-arm starts the same scan in
; sc_mode 2, which stops only at the matching end. Either way the scan steps over immediates,
; so a 0x05 or 0x0B inside a constant is never a delimiter. A call saves one frame (return
; pc, operand height, label height, run window, locals count) on a call stack of CALL_MAX
; frames and moves the callee's parameters into a fresh window of LOCALS entries in the one
; flat array loc[LOCALS_TOTAL], addressed from lbase; the callee runs in its own window of the
; code page (run_base / run_len), so a function body is code like any other and pc stays
; relative. return, and the function-level end, restore the caller with the callee's top of
; stack as the result when a frame is open, and end the run when none is. Labels the callee
; pushes sit above lbl (the caller's label height) and br out of the function body answers
; ERR_LABEL. The function table fn_off/fn_np/fn_nl/fn_ty, the element table elem and the
; globals glob are cell arrays loaded over the wire with OP_LOAD_TABLES. Fuel stays one unit
; per fetch, so a recursion with no base case ends with ERR_CALL at CALL_MAX deep (or
; ERR_FUEL), and the next request starts clean. Nothing of P6 was synthesised or run on the
; board.
; -
; THE WIRE. The TRI-NET node link, the one that carried 1035886/1035886 TNF16 requests and
; 251616/251616 mxdot4 requests at 1144744 baud with none lost: CFGMCLK between 65.6 and
; 68.7 MHz, divider 60, one start bit, 8 data bits LSB first, one stop bit.
;   Request  SYNC0 SYNC1 OP SEQ SA SB A0..A15 B0..B15            38 bytes
;   OP is a program id, SEQ is echoed, SA SB and A4..A15 B4..B15 are zero, and the operands
;   are x = A0..A3 little-endian and y = B0..B3 little-endian, both raw u32 with no range
;   limit: the LEB range limits only constants inside program bodies.
;   Response RESP_OK SEQ y0 y1 y2                                5 bytes
;   The word on the wire is the low 24 bits of the u32 result, little-endian. The engine is
;   full 32-bit inside; 24 bits is the response width of this link. Board vectors come in two
;   kinds: exact vectors, whose full result already fits the word, and low-24 vectors (the
;   wraparound and the negative-constant programs), where the golden is the low 24 bits of the
;   full u32 and full-width exactness stays pinned by the MVP spec in simulation.
;   An unknown OP or any engine error (bad opcode, stack underflow or overflow, local index,
;   LEB continuation, program counter past end, label out of range, fuel spent, memory access
;   outside the page, call depth past CALL_MAX, a function index past the table or naming an
;   empty row, a call_indirect element or type mismatch, a global index past the array, or a
;   LOAD_TABLES row out of range) answers RESP_BADOP SEQ 0 0 0.
; -
; WHAT A PASS SAYS. This RTL receives real WASM program ids and operands over a UART, executes
; one WASM opcode per clock, and answers with the exact result, on this board, for every
; vector listed here, against a golden built by the host runner from the same program bytes.
; WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. Nothing about speed beyond one opcode per clock (a taken branch is
; two engine steps plus one per skipped byte), nothing about programs outside the opcode set
; named above, and nothing about formats: the response word is 24 bits by the wire, not by
; the engine.
; ASCII only, English only.

module fpga_wasm_board;

pub const KIND : str = "board-cell";
pub const ID : str = "fpga/wasm_board_ax7203";
pub const EPIC : str = "gHashTag/trinity-fpga#917";

; --- Board ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const BOARD : str = "ALINX AX7203";
pub const PART : str = "xc7a200tfbg484-2";
pub const IDCODE : u32 = 325279891;
pub const TOP : str = "wasm_board_ax7203";
pub const XDC : str = "trinity-fpga specs/fpga/constraints/gf16_clean_ax7203.xdc";

; --- Wire, the TRI-NET node link (tnf16_on_board_ax7203.t27, mxdot4_on_board_ax7203.t27) --
pub const UART_SOURCE : str = "self; the receiver and transmitter are this spec";
pub const BAUD_DIV : u32 = 60;
pub const HOST_BAUD : u32 = 1144744;
pub const CP2102N_REF_HZ : u32 = 24000000;
pub const CP2102N_N : u32 = 21;
pub const WIRE_BAUD : u32 = 1142857;
pub const CFGMCLK_MIN_HZ : u32 = 65600000;
pub const CFGMCLK_MAX_HZ : u32 = 68700000;

; --- Frame ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const SYNC0 : u8 = 170;
pub const SYNC1 : u8 = 85;
pub const RESP_OK : u8 = 165;
pub const RESP_BADOP : u8 = 229;
pub const REQ_BYTES : u32 = 38;
pub const BODY_BYTES : u32 = 36;
pub const RESP_BYTES : u8 = 5;
pub const WORD_BITS : u8 = 24;
pub const X_OFF : u32 = 4;
pub const Y_OFF : u32 = 20;

; --- P2 wire program store: OP_LOAD_PAGE writes a page of code, OP_RUN_USER runs from it
pub const OP_LOAD_PAGE : u8 = 0xFE;
pub const OP_RUN_USER : u8 = 0xFD;
pub const CODE_PAGES : u32 = 4;
pub const PAGE_BYTES : u32 = 32;

; --- Machine ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const STACK_MAX : u32 = 16;
pub const LOCALS : u32 = 4;
pub const CODE_BYTES : u32 = 101;
pub const CODE_PAD : u32 = 128;
pub const I32_MASK : u64 = 0xFFFFFFFF;

; --- control flow (issue #12010): a label stack of LABEL_MAX frames, one LEB byte per label,
; FUEL_MAX fetches per run so a looping program cannot hang the link
pub const OP_BLOCK : u8 = 0x02;
pub const OP_LOOP : u8 = 0x03;
pub const OP_BR : u8 = 0x0C;
pub const OP_BR_IF : u8 = 0x0D;
pub const OP_BR_TABLE : u8 = 0x0E;
pub const BT_VOID : u8 = 0x40;
pub const BT_I32 : u8 = 0x7F;
pub const LABEL_MAX : u32 = 8;
pub const FUEL_MAX : u32 = 65536;

; --- P6 (issue #12323): if/else, call frames, call_indirect, globals --------------------
; opcode bytes are the WebAssembly MVP finals; OP_LOAD_TABLES is a wire op like OP_LOAD_PAGE.
; Sizes: CALL_MAX frames, LOCALS_TOTAL flat local entries (CALL_MAX windows of LOCALS), a
; function table of FUNC_MAX rows, an element table of ELEM_MAX slots, GLOBAL_MAX globals.
; NO_FUNC marks an empty function row and an empty element slot.
pub const OP_IF : u8 = 0x04;
pub const OP_ELSE : u8 = 0x05;
pub const OP_CALL : u8 = 0x10;
pub const OP_CALL_INDIRECT : u8 = 0x11;
pub const OP_GLOBAL_GET : u8 = 0x23;
pub const OP_GLOBAL_SET : u8 = 0x24;
pub const OP_LOAD_TABLES : u8 = 0xFC;
pub const CALL_MAX : u32 = 4;
pub const LOCALS_TOTAL : u32 = 20;
pub const FUNC_MAX : u32 = 8;
pub const ELEM_MAX : u32 = 4;
pub const GLOBAL_MAX : u32 = 4;
pub const NO_FUNC : u8 = 255;

; --- opcodes, WebAssembly MVP final bytes (pinned by test opcode_bytes_are_real_wasm) ----
pub const OP_END : u8 = 0x0B;
pub const OP_RETURN : u8 = 0x0F;
pub const OP_DROP : u8 = 0x1A;
pub const OP_SELECT : u8 = 0x1B;
pub const OP_LOCAL_GET : u8 = 0x20;
pub const OP_LOCAL_SET : u8 = 0x21;
pub const OP_LOCAL_TEE : u8 = 0x22;
pub const OP_I32_CONST : u8 = 0x41;
; P3 (2026-10-24): i64.const joined as the LOW-32 floor. It decoded the same
; five-byte SLEB128 submachine as OP_I32_CONST and pushed one u32 word. P7 (#12371)
; replaces that floor with a real pair: OP_I64_CONST now pushes TWO stack slots, the
; HIGH word deeper and the LOW word on top, decodes up to ten SLEB bytes, and refuses
; a continuation on the tenth byte with ERR_LEB. The root end still answers
; st[sp - 1], now the LOW word of the i64 on top, so the P3 answers stand (987654321
; answers B1 68 DE, -5 answers FB FF FF).
pub const OP_I64_CONST : u8 = 0x42;
; P7 (#12371): the nine i64 bytes the cell executes on the pair layout. Every one
; works on i64 values held as two consecutive u32 slots, HIGH deeper, LOW on top.
; Only the low-24-bit answer window and the 32-bit words of the stack ever exist in
; the datapath: no u64 value beyond 32 bits is formed (the t27c Verilog emitter
; emits an as u64 cast verbatim, #12296), so a carry is detected as sum < operand
; and a borrow as a < b, never by a shift of a wide sum.
pub const OP_I32_WRAP_I64 : u8 = 0xA7;
pub const OP_I64_EXTEND_I32_S : u8 = 0xAC;
pub const OP_I64_EXTEND_I32_U : u8 = 0xAD;
pub const OP_I64_ADD : u8 = 0x7C;
pub const OP_I64_SUB : u8 = 0x7D;
pub const OP_I64_MUL : u8 = 0x7E;
pub const OP_I64_SHL : u8 = 0x86;
pub const OP_I64_SHR_S : u8 = 0x87;
pub const OP_I64_SHR_U : u8 = 0x88;
; P4 (2026-10-24): the float consts join as RAW-BIT words -- no LEB at all. A real
; wasm f32.const carries its four IEEE-754 bytes little-endian right after the
; opcode, f64.const its eight; the floor pushes those bits as the u32 stack word:
; f32 wholesale, f64 as the low 32 (its first four bytes), the same honest floor
; as i64.const. Float arithmetic and the f64 high half stay a separate increment.
pub const OP_F32_CONST : u8 = 0x43;
pub const OP_F32_ADD : u8 = 0x92;
pub const OP_F32_SUB : u8 = 0x93;
pub const OP_F32_MUL : u8 = 0x94;
pub const OP_F64_CONST : u8 = 0x44;
pub const OP_I32_EQZ : u8 = 0x45;
pub const OP_I32_EQ : u8 = 0x46;
pub const OP_I32_NE : u8 = 0x47;
pub const OP_I32_LT_S : u8 = 0x48;
pub const OP_I32_LT_U : u8 = 0x49;
pub const OP_I32_GT_S : u8 = 0x4A;
pub const OP_I32_GT_U : u8 = 0x4B;
pub const OP_I32_LE_U : u8 = 0x4D;
pub const OP_I32_LE_S : u8 = 0x4C;
pub const OP_I32_GE_U : u8 = 0x4F;
pub const OP_I32_GE_S : u8 = 0x4E;
pub const OP_I32_CLZ : u8 = 0x67;
pub const OP_I32_CTZ : u8 = 0x68;
pub const OP_I32_POPCNT : u8 = 0x69;
pub const OP_I32_ADD : u8 = 0x6A;
pub const OP_I32_SUB : u8 = 0x6B;
pub const OP_I32_MUL : u8 = 0x6C;
pub const OP_I32_DIV_S : u8 = 0x6D;
pub const OP_I32_DIV_U : u8 = 0x6E;
pub const OP_I32_REM_S : u8 = 0x6F;
pub const OP_I32_REM_U : u8 = 0x70;
pub const OP_I32_AND : u8 = 0x71;
pub const OP_I32_OR : u8 = 0x72;
pub const OP_I32_XOR : u8 = 0x73;
pub const OP_I32_SHL : u8 = 0x74;
pub const OP_I32_SHR_S : u8 = 0x75;
pub const OP_I32_SHR_U : u8 = 0x76;
pub const OP_I32_ROTL : u8 = 0x77;
pub const OP_I32_ROTR : u8 = 0x78;

; P5 (issue #12202): linear memory, one page of MEM_BYTES. A load or store carries a memarg
; (align, offset: two LEB128 u32); memory.size and memory.grow carry the reserved memory-index
; byte, which this cell requires to be 0.
pub const OP_I32_LOAD : u8 = 0x28;
pub const OP_I32_LOAD8_S : u8 = 0x2C;
pub const OP_I32_LOAD8_U : u8 = 0x2D;
pub const OP_I32_LOAD16_S : u8 = 0x2E;
pub const OP_I32_LOAD16_U : u8 = 0x2F;
pub const OP_I32_STORE : u8 = 0x36;
pub const OP_I32_STORE8 : u8 = 0x3A;
pub const OP_I32_STORE16 : u8 = 0x3B;
pub const OP_MEMORY_SIZE : u8 = 0x3F;
pub const OP_MEMORY_GROW : u8 = 0x40;
pub const MEM_BYTES : u32 = 65536;

; --- error codes (the MVP numbers; 4 was free and P2 gives it to divide-by-zero)
pub const ERR_NONE : u8 = 0;
pub const ERR_STACK : u8 = 1;
pub const ERR_LOCAL : u8 = 2;
pub const ERR_PC : u8 = 3;
pub const ERR_DIV : u8 = 4;
pub const ERR_OPCODE : u8 = 5;
pub const ERR_LEB : u8 = 6;
pub const ERR_PROG : u8 = 7;
pub const ERR_LABEL : u8 = 8;
pub const ERR_FUEL : u8 = 9;
pub const ERR_MEM : u8 = 10;
; P6 (issue #12323): call depth, function index, element or type mismatch, global index
pub const ERR_CALL : u8 = 11;
pub const ERR_FUNC : u8 = 12;
pub const ERR_TYPE : u8 = 13;
pub const ERR_GLOBAL : u8 = 14;

; --- programs: the straight-line bodies of the MVP, byte for byte ------------------------
pub const ID_ADD_DOUBLE : u8 = 0;
pub const ID_ANSWER : u8 = 1;
pub const ID_XMUL_NOT : u8 = 2;
pub const ID_SUB_AND_OR : u8 = 3;
